Compiling/Installing
====================

Binary Installation
-------------------

Use the binary package  and default package installation method for your
system:

* Arch
  - Pacman
* Debian
  - dpkg
* Fedora
  - yum
* Slackware
  - installpkg
* FreeBSD
  - Ports
* Solaris
  - pkg
* Windows
  - The executable installer
* OS X
  - The pkg installer
* Andoird
  - The Google Play Store


Compiling from Source
---------------------

### Dependencies

To compile from source you will need the following:

* cmake
* pkgconfig
* GTK (version 3 or newer)
* libgcrypt
* liblzma
* libcurl
* pthreads
* cmocka (for tests)


### Linux / FreeBSD / Solaris

Most of the above are installed as part of the base (or core) OS on many
distributions (but not always).

    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build

### For non-GNU/Linux

For Microsoft Windows and Apple's macOS there are a few prerequisites to
get a suitable build environment together, but then the instructions are
the same as above.

#### Microsoft Windows

* Install MSYS2 --- https://www.msys2.org/
* Install all of the above dependencies using MSYS2

#### Apple's macOS

* Install MacPorts --- https://www.macports.org/
* Install all of the above dependencies using MacPorts. GTK will need to
  use the options: +Quartz -x11
* Final step to bundle the dependencies into the application:

    cmake --install build --prefix "$PWD/stage"

#### Android

* gnu-crypto.jar
* xz-1.0.jar
* Android File Dialog - http://code.google.com/p/android-file-dialog/
